<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="center"> 
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" align="center" width="640" class="st-wrapper st-wrapper-background st-module-wrapper-table" style="width: 640px;"> 
<tbody>
<tr> 
<td width="100%" bgcolor="#DCEAF6" valign="top" style="width: 100%; padding-right: 39px; padding-left: 41px;"> 
<table role="presentation" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" align="center" width="100%" style="width: 100%;"> 
<tbody>
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left"> 
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="560" class="st-mso-full-width st-mobile-full-width" style="width: 560px;"> 
<tbody>
<tr> 
<td align="center" valign="top" width="560"> 
<table width="100%" border="0" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" role="presentation"> 
<tbody>
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="center" style="padding: 0px; width: 100%;"> <p height="20" width="100%" style="mso-line-height-rule:exactly; mso-table-lspace:0pt; mso-table-rspace:0pt; text-size-adjust:100%; width: 100%; height: 20px; max-height: 20px; margin: 0px; font-size: 20px; line-height: 20px"> &nbsp; </p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 27px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 29px; padding-bottom: 20px; width: 100%;"> <p style="text-align: left; margin: 0px;"><span style="color: #0f476b; font-size: 27px; line-height: 29px;">Payment Requests:</span></p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> 
<ul style="margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-top: 0px !important;"> 
<li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">Within the Payment Request flow, clients can generate a real-time quote for the amount their payer will pay in their local currency for the chosen payment method. This quote is held for 30 minutes and helps provide payers the exact amount they’d pay through Flywire. This is a feature flag that can be enabled by your RM or by reaching out to <span style="color: #147bd1;"><a style="color: #147bd1;" href="mailto:travel_operations@flywire.com"><strong><u>travel_operations@flywire.com</u></strong></a></span>.</li> 
<li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">Clients can now create and save custom templates for importing payment requests with fields such as due date and expiration date. You can find this under Import/Export settings &gt;&gt; payment requests.</li> 
<li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">Within a payment request, the request to store the payment method for that contact now appears when creating a payment request for installments and subscriptions. This can be used by you in the event the payer needs to be charged at a later date.</li> 
<li style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px;">New filtering options to filter by payment method for installments and one-time payment requests are now available. Please reach out to your RM if you’d like to enable these filters.</li> 
</ul> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
</tbody>
</table> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
